shtab automatically generates shell tab completion scripts for Python
CLI applications.  It takes an argparse.ArgumentParser object and
writes a static completion script for bash, zsh, tcsh, fish, or
PowerShell.

Because the script is generated ahead of time, completion normally
does not need to start the Python application on every key press,
unlike argcomplete.

shtab can be used as a library, to add a --print-completion option to
an application, or through the shtab command, which works on any
importable parser (also click based ones, and docopt via argopt).
